other in these events in a best of three competition. Players take turns completing each task until a winner is declared.\n\nLicense Mode provides a series of timed tests (like knocking over poles, parking and digging sand) that must be completed in order to gain your operator's license.\n\nThe Level Editor lets players design their own courses on a 6 x 6 grid, with obstacles such as holes, electric fences, cones, and sheds. The three available shovels vary in their size, speed, capacity, and digging ability. In each event, players have the option of a first- or third-person perspective.", "themes": [{"id": 1, "name": "Action"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/power-shovel", "videos": [{"id": 38636, "name": "Gameplay Video", "video_id": "lZ4DfREkWxA", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lZ4DfREkWxA", "title": "Power Shovel (PS1) Playthrough - NintendoComplete", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/lZ4DfREkWxA/maxresdefault.jpg"}, {"id": 169069, "name": "Gameplay Video", "video_id": "Ro_cTqjokrE", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ro_cTqjokrE", "title": "Intro POWER SHOVEL SIMULATOR arcade de Taito.", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Ro_cTqjokrE/maxresdefault.jpg"}], "collections": [{"id": 2194, "name": "Simple 1500"}]}